The binary number system is a base-2 numeral system that uses only two symbols: 0 and 1. Each digit in a binary number is called a bit (binary digit). While humans primarily use the base-10 decimal system (0-9) because we have ten fingers, computers use binary because their hardware consists of electronic circuits that can exist in only two states: on (1) or off (0).
Converting Binary 0101 to Decimal
To convert the binary number 0101 to a decimal number, you multiply each bit by 2 raised to the power of its position (starting from 0 on the far right), and then add the results together.

